From e62ee6bacae0c2252445956dbdfffd164eea3b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfry <belfry@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:05:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Belfry: guests, a key put in a group without relay membership
 reads and writes there only

With [groups] guests = true, a key that isn't a relay member but whose latest
kind 9000/9001 in a group is a 9000 may connect. It receives only its groups'
events (their state events included) and profiles, and writes only in its
groups (never moderation or creation) and its own profile. Anonymous readers
and other non-members keep the existing rules.
